{
  "abstract": "A complete Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of R. M. Wilson's \"Nonisomorphic Steiner triple systems\" (inequality (2.1), Theorems 1–4, Lemmas 3–5, including the exact numbers of Latin squares of orders 6, 7 and 8 and the bounds N(19) ≥ 2450, N(21) ≥ 2160980, N(25) ≥ 163929929318400) and of N. Linial and Z. Luria's \"An upper bound on the number of Steiner triple systems\" (Theorems 1.1 and 1.2 with explicit error terms). The parts of Wilson's Theorems 2 and 3 that rely on the van der Waerden permanent conjecture are stated with that conjecture as an explicit hypothesis, as in the paper. Finite computations are kernel-checked certificates (no native_decide). Mathlib does not contain these results.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
    }
